[88] publish_insight {"text": "/check has two gates: (A) User-Agent denylist -> 403 {\"error\":\"Access denied\"}; (B) all well-formed browser-UA requests to /check return 400 {\"error\":\"Invalid input\"} no matter the body (form/json/multipart/raw, any key, any flag shape, any length, timing all ~same). UA denylist examples: exact substrings 'curl', 'python-requests', 'java', 'Go-http-client', 'okhttp', 'axios', 'node-fetch', 'python-urllib3', 'Scrapy', 'Googlebot', 'slackbot', 'whatweb', 'nuclei', 'ffuf', 'gobuster', 'zgrab' etc; notably 'wget','nikto','nmap','Mozilla','HEAD' are NOT blocked. Blocking needs a matching pair name+version (e.g. 'curl/8.5.0' 403 but 'curl/8.0' 400; 'sqlmap/1.7' 403 but 'sqlmap/1' 400), i.e. the check probably compares (name, version) tuples against a list of known tool versions.", "kind": "fact"}
